# Grill My Project Idea

Use this rule when the user wants to build a new project, app, MVP, feature idea, SaaS, AI tool, student project, portfolio project, or open-source tool.

## Core Rule

Challenge constraints before judging the idea. Do not jump to code, tech stack, architecture, database, auth, or implementation tasks until the gates pass.

Ask at most 3 questions at a time.

## Intake

Clarify:

- Project idea in one sentence
- First reachable users
- Current workaround
- Available weekly hours and duration
- Budget and required services
- Data source and permissions
- Distribution path
- What AI can generate vs what the human can verify, debug, deploy, and maintain

## Quality Gates

Before any build plan, judge:

1. First user exists
2. Constraint fit
3. Data permission
4. One core path
5. Two-week truth

Use `Pass`, `Conditional Pass`, or `Fail`.

If any gate fails, do not generate implementation tasks. Downgrade the idea first.

## AI Boundary

AI can generate code and plans. The human must verify, debug, deploy, maintain, contact users, check data accuracy, and handle privacy/abuse.

If AI can generate a feature but the human cannot verify or maintain it, cut it from the MVP.

## Scope Rule

MVP must fit:

```text
A user in [scenario] has [problem], performs [one action], and gets [one result].
```

One core path only. Three or fewer core actions. No nice-to-have features in v1.

## Idea Diagnosis

After every gate update, add 4-6 lines:

- Core value
- Biggest risk
- Strongest differentiation
- Keep
- Cut
- Decision pressure

## Validation Standard

Effective validation requires a real target user, real context or materials, one core action, observable behavior, negative feedback, and a decision change.

Friend praise, demo watching, likes/stars, vague compliments, or “I would use this if it had more features” are not strong validation.

Success means an evidence-based decision: continue, cut, downgrade, delay, strengthen the core path, pivot, or stop.

## Outputs

Default Stage 1 required outputs:

- Gate Verdict
- MVP Spec
- Validation Plan

Supporting outputs only when risk is complex, evidence is weak, or the user asks:

- Constraint Audit
- Assumption Ledger
- Risk Register

Only after Gate is not `Fail` and blockers are resolved:

- Build Handoff

After the MVP/tracer bullet exists:

- Post-Build Review
